/-!
# Completion for Noetherian rings

Let `I` be an ideal of a commutative ring `R`, and assume that `R / I` is Noetherian and
that `I` is finitely generated.  Then the `I`-adic completion `R^∧ = AdicCompletion I R` is
a Noetherian ring, and it is complete with respect to `I R^∧ = I.map ι`, the ideal of `R^∧`
generated by the image of `I` under the structure map `ι = algebraMap R (AdicCompletion I R)`
(Stacks Lemma 10.97.5, tag `05GH`).

## Main results

* `noetherian_of_isAdicComplete_fg`: a commutative ring `S` that is complete with respect to
  a finitely generated ideal `J` and whose quotient `S / J` is Noetherian is itself
  Noetherian.
* `completion_noetherian`: the completion `R^∧` is Noetherian and `I R^∧`-adically complete.

## Background

* The `I`-adic completion `R^∧ := AdicCompletion I R` is the inverse limit `lim_n R / I^n`
  of the quotient rings, with its natural `CommRing` structure.
* The structure map is the canonical ring homomorphism `ι : R → R^∧`, given by
  `algebraMap R (AdicCompletion I R)`; it sends `r` to the compatible family of its
  residues `(r mod I^n)_n`.
* `I R^∧` is the ideal of `R^∧` generated by the image of `I` under `ι`, that is
  `Ideal.map (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion I R)) I`.
* `IsNoetherianRing S` means every ideal of `S` is finitely generated, equivalently the
  ascending chain condition holds.
* `IsAdicComplete J S` means `S` is both `J`-adically separated (`⋂_n J^n = 0`) and
  `J`-adically precomplete.
* `I.FG` means `I = (f_1, …, f_t)` for finitely many elements `f_i ∈ R`.

The conclusion is stated as a conjunction of Noetherianness and `I R^∧`-adic completeness,
matching the assertion that `R^∧` is a Noetherian ring complete with respect to `I R^∧`.

## Proof outline

Write `S := AdicCompletion I R = R^∧`, `ι := algebraMap R S` and `J := I.map ι = I·S`.

* Completeness of `S` with respect to `J` is Stacks 05GG, available in Mathlib as
  `AdicCompletion.isAdicComplete` (the completion is `I`-adically complete as a ring when
  `I` is finitely generated) together with `IsAdicComplete.map_algebraMap_iff`, which
  rewrites `IsAdicComplete (I.map ι) S` to `IsAdicComplete I S`.
* Noetherianness is the substantive half.  It reduces to the purely ring-theoretic
  statement `noetherian_of_isAdicComplete_fg`, instantiated at `S = R^∧` and `J = I·R^∧`
  using: `J.FG` (from `Ideal.FG.map`), completeness as above, and
  `IsNoetherianRing (S / J)`, which holds because `S / J ≅ R / I` — this is
  `completion_quot_noetherian`.

### The associated graded argument

Let `J = (g₁, …, g_t)` and form the associated graded ring `gr_J(S) = ⨁_{n≥0} Jⁿ / Jⁿ⁺¹`.
Sending the degree-`1` indeterminate `Tᵢ` to the class of `gᵢ` in `J / J²` defines a
surjection of graded `(S/J)`-algebras `(S/J)[T₁, …, T_t] ↠ gr_J(S)`: the `gᵢ` generate `J`,
hence their classes generate `gr_J(S)` as an `(S/J)`-algebra.  Since `S/J` is Noetherian,
`(S/J)[T₁, …, T_t]` is Noetherian by the Hilbert basis theorem
(`MvPolynomial.isNoetherianRing`), so its quotient `gr_J(S)` is Noetherian as well.

Now let `K ⊆ S` be any ideal.  Consider the induced filtration `K ∩ Jⁿ` and the homogeneous
ideal `gr(K) := ⨁_n (K ∩ Jⁿ) / (K ∩ Jⁿ⁺¹) ⊆ gr_J(S)`.  As `gr_J(S)` is Noetherian, `gr(K)`
is generated by finitely many homogeneous elements; lift these to elements `x₁, …, x_m ∈ K`
with `xⱼ ∈ K ∩ J^{dⱼ}`.  Given `y ∈ K`, one approximates `y` by `S`-linear combinations of
the `xⱼ` modulo successively higher powers of `J`: at each stage the leading form of the
remainder lies in `gr(K)` and hence is a combination of the leading forms of the `xⱼ`, so
the remainder can be pushed into a higher `Jⁿ`.  Because `S` is `J`-adically complete
(Hausdorff and precomplete), this Cauchy process converges and realizes `y` as an `S`-linear
combination of the `xⱼ`.  Hence every ideal of `S` is finitely generated.

### How the graded object is realized here

Mathlib has no associated-graded-ring-of-a-filtration construction, so the graded object is
built directly, and as a *module* rather than a ring: `grPiece S J n` is the degree-`n`
leading-form space `Jⁿ / Jⁿ⁺¹` and `grModule S J = ⨁ₙ grPiece S J n`.  Given generators
`a : Fin t → S` of `J`, it becomes a module over `P := MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)` with
`Xᵢ` acting by multiplication by `aᵢ` on leading forms (`mulA`, `grModulePModule`).  It is
generated by the single degree-`0` element `1 + J`, hence — `P` being Noetherian by the
Hilbert basis theorem — is a Noetherian `P`-module (`grModule_noetherian`).

The leading forms of an ideal `K` span a `P`-submodule of `grModule S J`, which is therefore
finitely generated; lifting homogeneous generators to `fₖ ∈ K ∩ J^(dₖ)` and reading off
`S`-coefficients degree by degree yields the *approximation property*

  `∀ N x, x ∈ K → x ∈ J^N → ∃ s, (∀ k, s k ∈ J^(N - d k)) ∧ x - ∑ k, s k * f k ∈ J^(N+1)`

for that finite family (`leadingForm_core`, `leadingForm_fg`, `gradedLeading_fg`,
`exists_leading_generators`, `exists_approx_generators`).  Completeness then converts the
approximation property into finite generation of `K`: iterating it (telescoping) builds, for
each `k`, a `J`-Cauchy partial-sum sequence `σ_k^{(M)} = ∑_{N≤M} s_k^{(N)}`; precompleteness
(`IsPrecomplete.prec'`) yields limits `cₖ`, and the remainder lies in `⋂ₙ Jⁿ`, which is `0`
by the Hausdorff property (`IsHausdorff.haus'`).  Hence `K = (f₁, …, f_r)`
(`fg_of_approx_generators`).
-/

@[expose] public section


open AdicCompletion

/-- The degree-`n` leading-form space `J^n / J^{n+1}`, realized as the quotient of
the `S`-submodule `J^n ⊆ S` by (the restriction of) `J^{n+1}`. -/
@[ega "0 10.1.1" "partial", ega "0 19.5.6.2", sga "1 II 4.14", sga "1 III 6.9"]
noncomputable abbrev grPiece (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ) : Type _ :=
  (J ^ n : Ideal S) ⧸ (Submodule.comap (J ^ n : Ideal S).subtype (J ^ (n + 1) : Ideal S))

/-- The associated-graded `S`-module `M = ⨁ₙ J^n/J^{n+1}` of the `J`-adic
filtration.  Once generators of `J` are fixed it carries a
`MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)`-module structure (`grModulePModule`) making it finitely
generated, hence Noetherian (`grModule_noetherian`). -/
@[ega "0 10.1.1" "partial",
  ega "0 15.1.5" "special case",
  ega "0 16.2.1" "special case",
  ega "III 4.3.13" "partial",
  ega "IV 19.6.1" "special case",
  ega "IV 6.10.1" "special case", sga "1 II 4.14", sga "7 X 2.14" "special case"]
noncomputable abbrev grModule (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) : Type _ :=
  DirectSum ℕ (fun n => grPiece S J n)

/-- Multiplication-by-`b` (for `b ∈ J^n`) as an `S`-linear map `J^m → J^(m+n)`.
A building block for the degree-shift maps on the associated-graded module:
`b * z ∈ J^(m+n)` since `b ∈ J^n`, `z ∈ J^m`. -/
noncomputable def grMulMap (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ) (b : S)
    (hb : b ∈ J ^ n) (m : ℕ) : (J ^ m : Ideal S) →ₗ[S] (J ^ (m + n) : Ideal S) where
  toFun := fun z => ⟨b * z, by
    rw [pow_add, mul_comm (J ^ m) (J ^ n)]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul hb z.property⟩
  map_add' x y := by
    ext
    simp [mul_add]
  map_smul' c x := by
    ext
    simp only [SetLike.val_smul, smul_eq_mul, RingHom.id_apply]
    ring

/-- The degree-`+n` shift map `grPiece S J m →ₗ[S] grPiece S J (m+n)` induced by
multiplication by `b ∈ J^n` on leading forms.  It is well defined because
`b · J^(m+1) ⊆ J^(m+n+1)`.  Taking `b = aᵢ` and `n = 1` gives the degree-`+1`
action of the indeterminate `Tᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def grShift (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ) (b : S)
    (hb : b ∈ J ^ n) (m : ℕ) : grPiece S J m →ₗ[S] grPiece S J (m + n) := by
  unfold grPiece
  refine Submodule.mapQ _ _ (grMulMap S J n b hb m) ?_
  intro z hz
  simp only [Submodule.mem_comap] at hz ⊢
  change b * (z : S) ∈ (J ^ (m + n + 1) : Ideal S)
  have h : b * (z : S) ∈ (J ^ n) * (J ^ (m + 1)) := Ideal.mul_mem_mul hb hz
  rw [← pow_add] at h
  exact Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (by omega) h

/-- The leading-form class in `grPiece S J n = J^n/J^{n+1}` of an element of `J^n`. -/
noncomputable def grMk (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ)
    (x : (J ^ n : Ideal S)) : grPiece S J n :=
  Submodule.Quotient.mk x

/-! ### The `S ⧸ J`-module structure on the associated-graded pieces -/

/-- The ideal `J` annihilates every leading-form piece `grPiece S J n`: for
`c ∈ J` and `x : grPiece S J n`, `c • x = 0`.  (If `x = z + J^{n+1}` with
`z ∈ J^n`, then `c * z ∈ J · J^n = J^{n+1}`.) -/
@[ega "IV 6.10.1" "special case"]
lemma grPiece_ann (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ) :
    ∀ (c : S) (x : grPiece S J n), c ∈ J → c • x = 0 := by
  intro c x hc
  unfold grPiece at x ⊢
  induction x using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
  | _ z =>
    rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
    simp only [Submodule.mem_comap]
    change c * (z : S) ∈ (J ^ (n + 1) : Ideal S)
    have : c * (z : S) ∈ J * J ^ n := Ideal.mul_mem_mul hc z.property
    rwa [← pow_succ'] at this

/-- The `S ⧸ J`-module structure on `grPiece S J n`, built by lifting the
`S`-action through `S ⧸ J` (legitimate because `J` annihilates `grPiece S J n`,
see `grPiece_ann`).  By construction `(Ideal.Quotient.mk J c) • x = c • x`
(`grPiece_smul_mk`), so the `S`-action factors through this one
(`grPieceTower`). -/
noncomputable instance grPieceModuleSJ (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ) :
    Module (S ⧸ J) (grPiece S J n) :=
  Module.compHom (grPiece S J n)
    (Ideal.Quotient.lift J (Module.toAddMonoidEnd S (grPiece S J n)) (fun c hc => by
      ext x
      simp only [Module.toAddMonoidEnd, AddMonoid.End.zero_apply]
      change c • x = 0
      exact grPiece_ann S J n c x hc))

/-- The `S ⧸ J`-action of `Ideal.Quotient.mk J c` on a leading-form piece agrees
with the `S`-action of `c` (definitional, by construction of `grPieceModuleSJ`). -/
lemma grPiece_smul_mk (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ) (c : S)
    (x : grPiece S J n) : (Ideal.Quotient.mk J c) • x = c • x := rfl

/-- The `S`-action on `grPiece S J n` factors through the `S ⧸ J`-action:
`(s • q) • x = s • (q • x)`. -/
noncomputable instance grPieceTower (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n : ℕ) :
    IsScalarTower S (S ⧸ J) (grPiece S J n) := by
  refine ⟨fun s q x => ?_⟩
  induction q using Quotient.inductionOn' with
  | h c =>
    change (s • (Ideal.Quotient.mk J c)) • x = s • ((Ideal.Quotient.mk J c) • x)
    rw [grPiece_smul_mk]
    have : s • (Ideal.Quotient.mk J c) = Ideal.Quotient.mk J (s * c) := by
      rw [map_mul, Algebra.smul_def]; rfl
    rw [this, grPiece_smul_mk, mul_smul]

/-- The total associated-graded module `grModule S J = ⨁ₙ grPiece S J n` is a
`S ⧸ J`-module (the direct sum of the `S ⧸ J`-module pieces). -/
@[ega "0 16.2.1" "special case", ega "IV 6.10.1" "special case"]
noncomputable instance grModuleModuleSJ (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) :
    Module (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J) := by unfold grModule; infer_instance

/-- The `S`-action on `grModule S J` factors through its `S ⧸ J`-action. -/
noncomputable instance grModuleTower (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) :
    IsScalarTower S (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J) := by unfold grModule; infer_instance

/-! ### The multiplication-by-`aᵢ` endomorphisms and their commuting -/

/-- A generator `aᵢ` of `J` lies in `J^1` (since `aᵢ ∈ range a ⊆ span (range a) = J`). -/
lemma mulA_hai (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i : Fin t) : a i ∈ J ^ 1 := by
  rw [pow_one, ha]; exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-- The action of the degree-1 indeterminate `Tᵢ` on the associated-graded module:
the total multiplication-by-`aᵢ` endomorphism `grModule S J →ₗ[S] grModule S J`,
assembled from the degree-`+1` shift maps `grShift S J 1 (a i)` on each piece. -/
noncomputable def mulA (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i : Fin t) :
    grModule S J →ₗ[S] grModule S J :=
  DirectSum.toModule S ℕ (DirectSum ℕ (fun n => grPiece S J n))
    (fun m => (DirectSum.lof S ℕ (fun n => grPiece S J n) (m + 1)).comp
      (grShift S J 1 (a i) (mulA_hai S J t a ha i) m))

/-- Evaluation of `mulA` on a single homogeneous element `lof m x`. -/
lemma mulA_lof (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i : Fin t) (m : ℕ) (x : grPiece S J m) :
    mulA S J t a ha i (DirectSum.lof S ℕ (fun n => grPiece S J n) m x)
      = DirectSum.lof S ℕ (fun n => grPiece S J n) (m + 1)
          (grShift S J 1 (a i) (mulA_hai S J t a ha i) m x) :=
  DirectSum.toModule_lof S m x

/-- The shift map acts on a leading-form class `grMk` by multiplication
(definitional unfolding of `grShift`/`grMulMap`). -/
lemma grShift_grMk (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (n m : ℕ) (b : S) (hb : b ∈ J ^ n)
    (z : (J ^ m : Ideal S)) :
    grShift S J n b hb m (grMk S J m z) = grMk S J (m + n) ⟨b * z, by
      rw [pow_add, mul_comm (J ^ m) (J ^ n)]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul hb z.2⟩ := by
  unfold grShift grMk grMulMap; rfl

/-- The degree-`+1` shift maps for two elements `b, c ∈ J^1` commute on each piece:
`grShift c (m+1) (grShift b m x) = grShift b (m+1) (grShift c m x)` (because
`c * (b * z) = b * (c * z)` in the commutative ring `S`). -/
lemma grShift_comm (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (m : ℕ) (b c : S)
    (hb : b ∈ J ^ 1) (hc : c ∈ J ^ 1) (x : grPiece S J m) :
    grShift S J 1 c hc (m + 1) (grShift S J 1 b hb m x)
      = grShift S J 1 b hb (m + 1) (grShift S J 1 c hc m x) := by
  unfold grPiece at x
  induction x using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
  | _ z =>
    change grShift S J 1 c hc (m + 1) (grShift S J 1 b hb m (grMk S J m z))
      = grShift S J 1 b hb (m + 1) (grShift S J 1 c hc m (grMk S J m z))
    rw [grShift_grMk, grShift_grMk, grShift_grMk, grShift_grMk]
    unfold grMk
    rw [Submodule.Quotient.eq]
    simp only [Submodule.mem_comap]
    change c * (b * z) - b * (c * z) ∈ _
    have : c * (b * z) - b * (c * z) = 0 := by ring
    rw [this]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _

/-- The composites of the two total endomorphisms `mulA i` and `mulA j` agree
(the `∘ₗ`-level commuting statement). -/
lemma mulA_comp_comm (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i j : Fin t) :
    (mulA S J t a ha i).comp (mulA S J t a ha j)
      = (mulA S J t a ha j).comp (mulA S J t a ha i) := by
  refine DirectSum.linearMap_ext _ fun m => LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  change mulA S J t a ha i (mulA S J t a ha j (DirectSum.lof S ℕ (fun n => grPiece S J n) m x))
    = mulA S J t a ha j (mulA S J t a ha i (DirectSum.lof S ℕ (fun n => grPiece S J n) m x))
  rw [mulA_lof, mulA_lof, mulA_lof, mulA_lof]
  congr 1
  exact grShift_comm S J m (a j) (a i) (mulA_hai S J t a ha j) (mulA_hai S J t a ha i) x

/-- The multiplication-by-`aᵢ` and multiplication-by-`aⱼ` endomorphisms of
`grModule S J` commute (`Commute (mulA … i) (mulA … j)`), reflecting `aᵢ aⱼ = aⱼ aᵢ`.
This is what permits making `grModule S J` a module over the polynomial ring
`MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)`. -/
lemma mulA_commute (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i j : Fin t) :
    Commute (mulA S J t a ha i) (mulA S J t a ha j) :=
  mulA_comp_comm S J t a ha i j

/-! ### The `MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)`-module structure on `grModule` -/

/-- The multiplication-by-`aᵢ` endomorphism as an `(S ⧸ J)`-linear map.  `mulA i`
is `S`-linear, and the `S`-action factors through `S ⧸ J` (scalar tower
`grModuleTower`), so it is automatically `(S ⧸ J)`-linear via
`LinearMap.extendScalarsOfSurjective` (using surjectivity of `Ideal.Quotient.mk`). -/
noncomputable def mulA' (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i : Fin t) :
    Module.End (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J) :=
  LinearMap.extendScalarsOfSurjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (mulA S J t a ha i)

/-- `mulA'` applied to `x` agrees with `mulA` applied to `x`. -/
lemma mulA'_apply (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i : Fin t) (x : grModule S J) :
    mulA' S J t a ha i x = mulA S J t a ha i x :=
  LinearMap.extendScalarsOfSurjective_apply _ _ _

/-- The `(S ⧸ J)`-linear multiplication endomorphisms commute. -/
lemma mulA'_commute (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i j : Fin t) :
    Commute (mulA' S J t a ha i) (mulA' S J t a ha j) := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  simpa only [Module.End.mul_apply, mulA'_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply] using
    LinearMap.ext_iff.mp (mulA_comp_comm S J t a ha i j) x

/-- The pairwise-commuting condition for `fun i => (mulA' i)^(μ i)` over `Fin t`. -/
lemma mulA'_pow_pairwise (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (μ : Fin t →₀ ℕ) :
    ((Finset.univ : Finset (Fin t)) : Set (Fin t)).Pairwise
      (Function.onFun Commute (fun i => (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ (μ i))) := by
  intro i _ j _ _
  exact (mulA'_commute S J t a ha i j).pow_pow _ _

/-- The monomial monoid-hom `g : Multiplicative (Fin t →₀ ℕ) →* Module.End`, sending
`μ` to the product `∏ i, (mulA' i)^(μ i)` (a `noncommProd`, valid since the factors
pairwise commute). -/
noncomputable def mulAMonoidHom (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) :
    Multiplicative (Fin t →₀ ℕ) →* Module.End (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J) where
  toFun μ := Finset.univ.noncommProd (fun i => (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd μ) i))
    (mulA'_pow_pairwise S J t a ha (Multiplicative.toAdd μ))
  map_one' := by
    rw [Finset.noncommProd_eq_pow_card (m := 1)]
    · rw [one_pow]
    · intro i _
      change (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((1 : Multiplicative (Fin t →₀ ℕ)) |>.toAdd i) = 1
      simp
  map_mul' := by
    intro μ ν
    change Finset.univ.noncommProd
        (fun i => (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd (μ * ν)) i)) _
      = Finset.univ.noncommProd (fun i => (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd μ) i)) _ *
        Finset.univ.noncommProd (fun i => (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd ν) i)) _
    rw [← Finset.noncommProd_mul_distrib
        (f := fun i => (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd μ) i))
        (g := fun i => (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd ν) i))
        (comm_ff := mulA'_pow_pairwise S J t a ha (Multiplicative.toAdd μ))
        (comm_gg := mulA'_pow_pairwise S J t a ha (Multiplicative.toAdd ν))
        (comm_gf := by
          intro i _ j _ _
          exact (mulA'_commute S J t a ha i j).pow_pow _ _)]
    apply Finset.noncommProd_congr rfl
    intro i _
    change (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd (μ * ν)) i)
      = (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd μ) i) *
        (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Multiplicative.toAdd ν) i)
    rw [← pow_add]
    rfl

-- needed: without it `mulAMonoidHom_single` fails: Tactic `rewrite` failed: Did not find an
-- occurrence of the pat…
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in
/-- Evaluation of the monomial monoid-hom on a single generator `single i 1`:
it returns `mulA' i`. -/
lemma mulAMonoidHom_single (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i : Fin t) :
    mulAMonoidHom S J t a ha (Multiplicative.ofAdd (Finsupp.single i 1)) = mulA' S J t a ha i := by
  classical
  change Finset.univ.noncommProd
      (fun j => (mulA' S J t a ha j) ^ ((Finsupp.single i 1 : Fin t →₀ ℕ) j))
      (mulA'_pow_pairwise S J t a ha (Finsupp.single i 1))
    = mulA' S J t a ha i
  set f : Fin t → Module.End (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J) :=
    fun j => (mulA' S J t a ha j) ^ ((Finsupp.single i 1 : Fin t →₀ ℕ) j) with hf
  have hcomm : ((Finset.univ : Finset (Fin t)) : Set (Fin t)).Pairwise
      (Function.onFun Commute f) := mulA'_pow_pairwise S J t a ha (Finsupp.single i 1)
  have huniv : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin t)) = insert i (Finset.univ.erase i) := by
    rw [Finset.insert_erase (Finset.mem_univ i)]
  have hcomm2 : ((Finset.univ.erase i : Finset (Fin t)) : Set (Fin t)).Pairwise
      (Function.onFun Commute f) := by
    intro x hx y hy hxy
    exact hcomm (Finset.mem_coe.mpr (Finset.mem_of_mem_erase (Finset.mem_coe.mp hx)))
      (Finset.mem_coe.mpr (Finset.mem_of_mem_erase (Finset.mem_coe.mp hy))) hxy
  rw [Finset.noncommProd_congr huniv (fun x _ => rfl) hcomm,
    Finset.noncommProd_insert_of_notMem _ _ _ _ (Finset.notMem_erase i _)]
  have hrest : (Finset.univ.erase i).noncommProd f hcomm2 = 1 := by
    rw [Finset.noncommProd_eq_pow_card (m := 1)]
    · rw [one_pow]
    · intro j hj
      have hji : j ≠ i := Finset.ne_of_mem_erase hj
      change (mulA' S J t a ha j) ^ ((Finsupp.single i 1 : Fin t →₀ ℕ) j) = 1
      have : (Finsupp.single i 1 : Fin t →₀ ℕ) j = 0 := by
        rw [Finsupp.single_apply, ite_eq_right (Ne.symm hji)]
      rw [this, pow_zero]
  rw [hrest, mul_one]
  change (mulA' S J t a ha i) ^ ((Finsupp.single i 1 : Fin t →₀ ℕ) i) = mulA' S J t a ha i
  rw [Finsupp.single_eq_same, pow_one]

/-- The ring hom `MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J) →+* Module.End (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J)`
encoding the polynomial action: `C c ↦ c • ·` and `Xᵢ ↦ mulA' i`.  Built via
`AddMonoidAlgebra.liftNCRingHom` from the central `algebraMap` and the monomial
monoid-hom `mulAMonoidHom`. -/
noncomputable def grModuleRingHom (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J) →+* Module.End (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J) :=
  AddMonoidAlgebra.liftNCRingHom
    (algebraMap (S ⧸ J) (Module.End (S ⧸ J) (grModule S J)))
    (mulAMonoidHom S J t a ha)
    (fun q μ => Algebra.commute_algebraMap_left q (mulAMonoidHom S J t a ha μ))

/-- The `MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)`-module structure on `grModule S J`, with
`p • x = (grModuleRingHom p) x`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def grModulePModule (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ)
    (a : Fin t → S) (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) :
    Module (MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)) (grModule S J) :=
  Module.compHom (grModule S J) (grModuleRingHom S J t a ha)

/-- The indeterminate `Xᵢ` acts on `grModule S J` by the multiplication-by-`aᵢ`
endomorphism `mulA i`. -/
lemma grModule_X_smul (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (i : Fin t) (x : grModule S J) :
    letI := grModulePModule S J t a ha
    (MvPolynomial.X i : MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)) • x = mulA S J t a ha i x := by
  change grModuleRingHom S J t a ha (MvPolynomial.X i) x = mulA S J t a ha i x
  have hX : (MvPolynomial.X i : MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J))
      = AddMonoidAlgebra.single (Finsupp.single i 1) 1 := rfl
  rw [hX, grModuleRingHom, AddMonoidAlgebra.liftNCRingHom_single]
  rw [mulAMonoidHom_single, map_one, one_mul]
  exact mulA'_apply S J t a ha i x

/-- The constant `C c` acts on `grModule S J` by the `(S ⧸ J)`-scalar `c`. -/
lemma grModule_C_smul (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (c : S ⧸ J) (x : grModule S J) :
    letI := grModulePModule S J t a ha
    (MvPolynomial.C c : MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J)) • x = c • x := by
  change grModuleRingHom S J t a ha (MvPolynomial.C c) x = c • x
  have hC : (MvPolynomial.C c : MvPolynomial (Fin t) (S ⧸ J))
      = AddMonoidAlgebra.single (0 : Fin t →₀ ℕ) c := rfl
  rw [hC, grModuleRingHom, AddMonoidAlgebra.liftNCRingHom_single]
  rw [show (Multiplicative.ofAdd (0 : Fin t →₀ ℕ)) = 1 from rfl, map_one, mul_one]
  rw [Module.algebraMap_end_apply]

/-- (★) Powers of `J` are spanned by the degree-`n` monomials in the generators.
This is the only place the generating family `a` (via `ha`) enters the leading-form
finiteness argument: it shows each `J^n` (hence each `grPiece S J n = J^n/J^{n+1}`)
is a *finitely generated* `S ⧸ J`-module, spanned by the (finitely many) monomials
`a^μ` with `|μ| = n`.  Proved by induction on `n` (`J^0 = ⊤ = span {1 = a^0}`; step
`J^(n+1) = J · J^n` via `pow_succ`, `Ideal.span_mul_span`, `ha`). -/
lemma star_pow_eq_span_monomials
    (S : Type*) [CommRing S] (J : Ideal S) (t : ℕ) (a : Fin t → S)
    (ha : J = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) (n : ℕ) :
    (J ^ n : Ideal S) = Ideal.span ((fun μ : Fin t →₀ ℕ => ∏ i, a i ^ μ i) ''
      {μ : Fin t →₀ ℕ | (μ.sum fun _ e => e) = n}) := by
  have hmon : ∀ (μ : Fin t →₀ ℕ) (j : Fin t),
      (fun ν : Fin t →₀ ℕ => ∏ i, a i ^ ν i) (μ + Finsupp.single j 1)
        = a j * (fun ν : Fin t →₀ ℕ => ∏ i, a i ^ ν i) μ := by
    intro μ j
    simp only
    simp_rw [Finsupp.add_apply, pow_add, Finset.prod_mul_distrib]
    rw [mul_comm]
    congr 1
    rw [Finset.prod_eq_single j]
    · rw [Finsupp.single_eq_same, pow_one]
    · intro i _ hi
      rw [Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne (Ne.symm hi).symm, pow_zero]
    · simp
  have hsum : ∀ (μ : Fin t →₀ ℕ) (j : Fin t),
      ((μ + Finsupp.single j 1).sum fun _ e => e) = (μ.sum fun _ e => e) + 1 := by
    intro μ j
    rw [Finsupp.sum_add_index (by intros; rfl) (by intros; rfl), Finsupp.sum_single_index rfl]
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    simp only [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
    have hset : {μ : Fin t →₀ ℕ | (μ.sum fun _ e => e) = 0} = {0} := by
      ext μ
      simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
      rw [Finsupp.sum, Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff]
      constructor
      · intro h
        ext i
        simp only [Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
        by_cases hi : i ∈ μ.support
        · exact h i hi
        · simpa using hi
      · intro h i hi
        simp [h] at hi
    rw [hset]
    simp only [Set.image_singleton, Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply, pow_zero,
      Finset.prod_const_one]
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_one]
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [pow_succ', ih, ha, Ideal.span_mul_span]
    congr 1
    ext x
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨y, ⟨i, rfl⟩, z, ⟨μ, hμ, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨μ + Finsupp.single i 1, ?_, ?_⟩
      · simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hμ ⊢
        rw [hsum, hμ]
      · rw [hmon]
    · rintro ⟨ν, hν, rfl⟩
      simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hν
      have hpos : 0 < ν.sum fun _ e => e := by rw [hν]; omega
      obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := (Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff (f := ν)).2 (by rintro rfl; simp at hpos)
      have hi1 : 1 ≤ ν i := by
        rw [Finsupp.mem_support_iff] at hi
        omega
      set μ := ν - Finsupp.single i 1 with hμdef
      have hνeq : ν = μ + Finsupp.single i 1 := by
        ext j
        simp only [hμdef, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.coe_tsub, Pi.sub_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
        by_cases h : i = j
        · subst h; simp; omega
        · simp [h]
      refine ⟨a i, ⟨i, rfl⟩, (fun ν : Fin t →₀ ℕ => ∏ k, a k ^ ν k) μ, ⟨μ, ?_, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
      · simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
        have := hsum μ i
        rw [← hνeq] at this
        omega
      · change a i * (fun ν : Fin t →₀ ℕ => ∏ k, a k ^ ν k) μ
          = (fun ν : Fin t →₀ ℕ => ∏ k, a k ^ ν k) ν
        rw [← hmon, ← hνeq]

end
